<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Protects the adhan audio from the release resource shrinker.

  NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS COMMENT: XML forbids a double hyphen anywhere
  inside a comment body, and AGP feeds this file straight to R8's XML parser.
  A stray "-" "-" pair here does not produce a friendly lint warning; it fails
  the whole minifyReleaseWithR8 task with an XMLStreamException six minutes
  into the build. Use an em dash instead, as below.

  azan.wav (5 MB, the single largest resource in this APK) is never named from
  Java, Kotlin or XML. Its only reference is a Dart string:

      static const String azanSoundName = 'azan';
      RawResourceAndroidNotificationSound(azanSoundName)

  Dart compiles to libapp.so, which the AGP resource shrinker does not scan.
  It only walks classes.dex and the resource table, so @raw/azan looks
  completely unreferenced in a release build and is a prime candidate for
  removal. When that happens the notification still posts, but the channel
  resolves a dead resource id and Android falls back to silence: banner
  appears, no adhan. Debug builds never shrink resources, which is why this
  only ever shows up in release.

  tools:keep is additive. It pins this one resource without disabling the
  shrinker's normal heuristics for everything else.

  If more sounds are added later (per-prayer adhan, takbir), extend the list:
      tools:keep="@raw/azan,@raw/takbir"
-->
<resources
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@raw/azan" />
